parameters.description:
**Order of the list, or an answered / unanswered / open cut.** Optional; default `latest`.

- `latest`  -  most recent activity first (a new answer, else the question itself  -  a years-old thread with a new
  answer is on top);
- `featured`  -  threads picked by the Houzz editors first, then the rest (the list still holds every thread, so
  `total` does not change);
- `popular`  -  most answers first;
- `unanswered`  -  only threads with no answer yet, newest first;
- `answered`  -  only threads with at least one answer, most recent activity first (the exact complement of
  `unanswered`);
- `open`  -  only threads still open, most recent activity first: leaves out the threads marked `resolved`, which
  every other order includes.

Does not apply to a `query` search (relevance order)  -  sending both is a 400.

